es verified from both nodes. The independently required provider-wide restart protocol was also fully and coherently demonstrated on all three nodes, with pre-restart baselines, reboot acknowledgements, distinct post-restart boot identities, and confirmed recovery of DNS service and resolution, corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is high; the only residue is a trivial /tmp/reboot.log artifact from the reboot mechanism on two nodes.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector's after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare was disabled), so no independent pre/post-prepare comparison was possible beyond what the executor itself captured.","Evidence for external upstream resolution relies on public domains (google.com) rather than a fully isolated test of upstream-only forwarding behavior, but this is a reasonable and sufficient proxy for the requirement."]},"ttft_ms":5184,"type":"result","duration_ms":74356,"uuid":"b1b41a47-1cd9-4b97-8692-be44b974c3e9","ttft_stream_ms":1275,"time_to_request_ms":52,"queued_turn_count":0}
